# Day 26/60 — AI Prior Authorization Workflow Simulator

## Objective

Today I built an AI-powered Prior Authorization Workflow Simulator to better understand how healthcare providers, patients, and insurance companies interact throughout the treatment approval process.

The application simulates each workflow stage, allowing users to experience approvals, denials, pending requests, and appeals in an interactive environment.

---

## What Was Generated

- AI Prior Authorization Workflow Simulator
- Interactive Patient Journey Tracker
- Document Submission Workflow
- Approval / Pending / Denial Scenarios
- Appeals Process Simulation
- Progress Dashboard
- Workflow Timeline
- Educational Process Summary

---

## What I Learned

### Healthcare Workflows Are Complex

Prior authorization involves multiple stakeholders, required documents, and several approval stages before treatment begins.

### User Experience Matters

Visualizing each workflow stage makes complex administrative processes much easier to understand.

### AI Accelerates Learning

Instead of only reading about healthcare workflows, AI helped create an interactive simulator that made the entire process easier to explore.

### Interactive Dashboards Improve Transparency

Real-time progress tracking helps users understand exactly where they are in a multi-step workflow.

---

## Skills Practiced

- Workflow Design
- Healthcare Process Simulation
- Dashboard Development
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- AI-Assisted Development

---

## Biggest Insight

The best applications simplify complicated systems and make them intuitive for everyone involved.

